WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/feedback/EmptyStateThreshold.tsx — a presentational, fully-controlled, non-error empty
  state for sections that only become useful at scale (e.g. a cost heatmap needs >= 30 sessions):
    EmptyStateThreshold({ currentCount, threshold, itemNoun?, sectionLabel, description?, message?, action?,
    className?, testId? }) renders a rounded-2xl, glass-bordered, surface-1/40 box (role="status"
    aria-live="polite") with a leading emerald CheckCircle2 (the section is HEALTHY, just waiting for more
    data — per the /charging redesign spec it is never silently hidden), a title row (h3 sectionLabel +
    a small muted Info glyph), an optional secondary description line, the message line
    (message ?? defaultMessage), and an optional CTA (action, e.g. "Adjust filters").
  Data sources (prompt): useTranslation only. The two t() keys, extracted verbatim:
    • emptyState.threshold.defaultItem  -> "items"   (the itemNoun fallback)
    • emptyState.threshold.message      -> "Need at least {{threshold}} {{noun}} to show meaningful patterns.
                                                       You have {{current}} so far." (i18next interpolation)
  Shared components used (prompt): none. Charts / maps used (prompt): none.
  Web test (__tests__/EmptyStateThreshold.test.tsx) pins: title renders; "at least 30 sessions" + "5 so far";
  default noun "items"; custom message wins (default absent); description renders; action renders;
  role=status + aria-live=polite. All reproduced natively (adapter + projection + a11y tests below).

SCOPE / ARCHITECTURE NOTE  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  The web component is the leaf empty-state itself: a controlled, presentational card with the only data
  dependency being useTranslation. This 0119 SHARED SURFACE reproduces it as the established P4 multi-state,
  data-bound HOST: it binds the controlled gate (counts + labels) through a P1/S8 source seam, renders every
  state, resolves chrome via the P1/S10 facade, uses the P1/S9 tokens, and emits the P1/S11 view.opened
  telemetry. The web card is the `.threshold` render branch; the P4 leaf contract adds loading / empty /
  error and the orthogonal connectivity axis (a freshness chip, never hiding the card). The CTA is gated on a
  wired handler exactly as the established AlertBanner (0113) surface gates its dismiss on `onClose`. No atomic
  shared component was needed (prompt "Out of Scope: Atomic shared components"); no Swift Charts / MapKit
  (web source has neither). The web `{{threshold}}/{{noun}}/{{current}}` interpolation is reproduced in the
  pure adapter so it is unit-tested without rendering.

